    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=6">Magazines</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>Ditch the Bitching.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P align=center><IMG src="http://www.madonnavillage.it/drownedmadonna/thegoss.png" border=0></P>
<P align=center><STRONG>today's editon of Daily Star</STRONG></P>
<P align=center><STRONG>Blimey. It looks like her new religious leanings really have changed Madonna for the better.<BR><BR></STRONG>The woman who once said:<STRONG> 'When I'm hungry, I eat. When I'm thirsty, I drink. When I feel like saying something, I say it,' seems to have put her old ways behind her - thanks to kabbala, the ancient religion she now follows. And she's trying to get others to do the same. <BR><BR>The star recently held an exclusive party at her London pad so that she could tell nine of her close personal showbiz chums that 'bitching is bad'. Her guests included Demi Moore and Ashton Kutcher and they were all treated to some words of Madonna wisdom.<BR><BR></STRONG>'She wanted to talk about an important part of kabbala: "Resisting evil impulses",' says an insider. 'Kabbalistically, the sin of murder is not limited to physical death - it also includes character assassination.<BR><BR><STRONG>'Madonna advised her friends that by simply switching the conversation from one person's bitterness towards something positive, it's the equivalent to saving someone's life.'<BR><BR>Apparently one of Madge's pals who has been particularly guilty of this sin is Britney Spears. And while we applaud Madonna's efforts to make the world a kinder place, we're not sure whether it's going to work. No bitching? In the entertainment industry? Is she kidding?!</STRONG></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
