 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=35">Life</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>£30 do? That's Ritch!</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><STRONG>From Bizarre / Sun:</STRONG></P><STRONG></STRONG><STRONG>
<P align=center><BR><IMG alt="user posted image" src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004421086,00.jpg" border=0><BR></STRONG><I>Just a regular Guy ... Ritchie dons hat for party</I><BR><BR><STRONG>MADONNA may be a multi-millionaire but I can reveal she’s not flashing her cash around.<BR></STRONG><BR>The Material Girl went back to basics when she threw <STRONG>a 36th birthday bash for hubby GUY RITCHIE at the weekend.<BR></STRONG><BR>And I mean basics. Madge paid £30 to hire a room at a London pub for Guy to have a knees-up with 20 of his closest friends, including nightclub entrepreneur PIERS ADAM.<BR><BR>Celebs were strictly off the guest list at Mayfair’s Punch Bowl for the Irish-themed party — as was the champagne.<BR><BR>Madge swilled half-pints of real ale and Guy stuck to Guinness.<BR><BR><BR><IMG alt="user posted image" src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004421093,00.jpg" border=0><BR><I>Cap in hand ... Madge is all smiles</I><BR><BR><STRONG>One guest said: “The party was great fun but not the type of do you’d expect Madonna to organise.<BR><BR>“She drank ale all night and really let her hair down. She had hired a two-piece Irish band and sang along to all the songs with everyone else.<BR><BR>“Madonna arrived with Guy at 9pm, looking a million miles from the star you see on stage. She was wearing baggy jeans, a flat cap and hardly any make-up.<BR></STRONG><BR>“She left by herself just before 1am and she was pretty merry — she loves the taste of ale and had a fair few.<BR><BR><IMG alt="user posted image" src="http://images.thesun.co.uk/picture/0,,2004421089,00.jpg" border=0><BR><I>Low-key ... Guy partied in pub</I><BR><BR>“She could’ve hired the Ritz and had champagne flowing all night but she knows what Guy likes.<BR><BR><STRONG>“Guy said it was the best night out he’s had in ages.<BR><BR></STRONG>“He stayed on until 3.30 and was in a right old state, telling all his pals how much he loved them and singing at the top of his voice.”<BR><BR>Oh dear, I wonder how many bottles of Kabbalah water it took to cure Mr Madonna’s hangover the next day?</P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
